@Playful121 Because our security model ASSUMES that any given hardware vendor has vulnerabilities and mitigates them by distributing keys across a diversity of vendors.

There is no such thing as guaranteed safety.

To be clear, if you're in a 2 of 3 setup you should not have 2 of the same device. You shouldn't have a signing threshold of keys generated / stored with the same hardware / software as that means you have potential for single point of failure.

